    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"padding-left:5px\"><div><div style=\"overflow:auto\"><div style=\"max-height:10000px\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m sorry if issue is already answered somewhere but I did not find anything helpful  yet.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Based on some other R object I would like to have a dynamic number of text inputs for the user (I want the number to depend on the number of topics for a topic model object). The idea let users assign labels for these topics via these text inputs. I already managed to somehow include the correct number of fields:</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">## server</font></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  output$selectInputs &lt;- renderUI({</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    w &lt;- &quot;&quot;</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    for(i in 1:ncol(props)) { # ncol(props) corresponds to the topics in another R object</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">      w &lt;- paste(w, textInput(paste(&quot;TL&quot;, i, sep = &quot;&quot;), paste(&quot;Topic &quot;, i, sep = &quot;&quot;), </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">                              value = as.character(i)))</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    }</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    HTML(w)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  })</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> ## ui</font></div></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">   htmlOutput(&quot;selectInputs&quot;)</font></div><div><br></div><div>But I am not able to store the values correctly using them in other outputs. I tried several versions of something like this:</div><div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  topiclabels &lt;- reactive({</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    topiclabels &lt;- list()</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    tlabs &lt;- str_extract_all(&#39;^TL&#39;, names(input))</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    for (i in tlabs) {</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">      topiclabels$i &lt;- input$i</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    }</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    return(topiclabels)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  })</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  observe({ # here I would like the choices for another input to be adjusted</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  updateSelectInput(session, &quot;topic&quot;, choices = topiclabels(),</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">                    selected=topiclabels()[1])</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  })</font></div></div><div><br></div><div>Can you please give me a hint on how to do this correctly? I&#39;m not sure whether htmlOutput is the correct way in the first place.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks and Cheers</div><div>Carsten</div></div></div></div></div><div></div><div></div></div><div><div style=\"margin-left:44px;padding-left:5px\"></div></div><div style=\"padding-left:5px\"><div style=\"padding-top:4px;padding-bottom:4px\"><div style=\"display:inline-block\"></div><div style=\"margin-top:4px;min-height:34px\"></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
